{title: By His Wounds We Are Healed}
{subtitle: Isaiah 53:5}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]A young shoot in [Bb]the dry ground
No beauty to draw our [Gm]eyes
He was despised and re[Eb]jected
A man of sorrows and [Bb]grief
We hid our faces from him
Holding him of [F/A]no ac[Gm]count
Yet he bore our hea[Eb]vy griefs
[F]Carrying our deep [Bb]sorrows
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But he was pierced for our trans[Eb]gressions
[F]Crushed for our iniqui[Bb]ties
[Gm]The punishment brought us [Eb]peace
Laid upon [F]his body
By his wounds we are [Gm]healed
[Eb]By his wounds we are [Bb]healed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
All of us have strayed like sheep
Turning to [F/A]our own [Gm]ways
The Lord laid all our [Eb]sin
Upon his innocent [Bb]soul
Oppressed and afflicted he stood
Yet did not [F/A]open [Gm]his mouth
Like a lamb to [Eb]the slaughter
[F]Silent before the [Bb]shearers
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But he was pierced for our trans[Eb]gressions
[F]Crushed for our iniqui[Bb]ties [Bbmaj7/A]
[Gm]The punishment brought us [Eb]peace
Laid upon [F]his body
By his wounds we are [Gm]healed
[Eb]By his wounds we are [Bb]healed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Taken by judgment and oppression
[F]Who gave it a thought in his gener[Gm]ation
Cut off from the land of the [Bb]living
Stricken for our transgres[Eb]sion
He who knew no sin was [F]led
To bear the weight of the world
[Gm]The curse that was ours became his
[Eb]The joy that is ours came from his pain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But he was pierced for our transgressions
[F]Crushed for our iniqui[Bb]ties
[Gm]The punishment brought us [Eb]peace
Laid upon [F]his body
By his wounds we are [Gm]healed
[Eb]By his wounds we are [Bb]healed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Healed by his [Eb]wounds
Pierced for our [Bb]sins
Healed by his [Eb][Bb]wounds
{end_of_verse}
